# Living Survey: cancer                                                                                              
                                                                                                                     
                                                                                                                     
                                                                                                                     
## Introduction                                                                                                      
                                                                                                                     
                                                                                                                     
                                                                                                                     
This document collects the scientific literature regarding **cancer**.                                               
                                                                                                                     
                                                                                                                     
                                                                                                                     
## Liquid Biopsy and Diagnostics                                                                                     
                                                                                                                     
Recent advances in non-invasive cancer detection have focused heavily on cell-free DNA (cfDNA) and nucleosome        
positioning. Research has established comprehensive atlases of nucleosome positioning signatures across repetitive   
elements in tumor tissues and cfDNA, demonstrating that these signatures can robustly discriminate healthy           
individuals from patients with various cancers, including colorectal, pancreatic, and glioblastoma (GBM)             
[^10.5526_err-00042900]. Similarly, analysis of nucleosome repositioning in paired normal/tumor brain tissues and    
corresponding cfDNA from GBM patients has identified specific transcription factors as potential biomarkers,         
highlighting the clinical potential of liquid biopsies for early detection [^10.5526_err-00042862].                  
                                                                                                                     
                                                                                                                     
                                                                                                                     
## Tumor Microenvironment and Metastasis                                                                             
                                                                                                                     
The spatial organization of the tumor microenvironment (TME) plays a critical role in metastasis and immune evasion. 
Single-cell and spatial multi-omics have revealed that clear cell renal cell carcinoma (ccRCC) lung metastases harbor
cancer-associated fibroblast lymphocyte exclusion sites that form a confined TME, directly impacting immune cell     
infiltration [^10.5281_zenodo.18767278][^10.5281_zenodo.18767279]. In parallel, large-scale spatially resolved       
atlases of pan-cancer brain metastases have been constructed, providing unprecedented insights into the cellular and 
spatial heterogeneity of metastatic niches across different primary tumor types                                      
[^10.5281_zenodo.21782884][^10.5281_zenodo.21782885][^10.5281_zenodo.21816284][^10.5281_zenodo.21816285].            
                                                                                                                     
                                                                                                                     
                                                                                                                     
## Metabolic and Nutritional Interventions                                                                           
                                                                                                                     
Metabolic reprogramming and nutritional interventions are emerging as potent strategies to induce cancer cell death. 
In prostate cancer, omega-3 polyunsaturated fatty acids (specifically EPA) have been shown to induce mitochondrial   
protein succinylation, disrupting mitochondrial homeostasis and triggering ferroptosis through GOT2                  
hyper-succinylation and SDHA modulation [^10.17638_03195029]. Similarly, in breast cancer, cyclic fasting and        
fasting-mimicking diets elevate plasma polyunsaturated fatty acids, which cooperate with nutrient starvation to      
induce lipid peroxidation and ferroptosis, offering a safe therapeutic strategy for triple-negative breast cancer    
[^10.21954_ou.ro.00108036].                                                                                          
                                                                                                                     
                                                                                                                     
                                                                                                                     
## Genomic and Transcriptomic Profiling                                                                              
                                                                                                                     
High-throughput sequencing continues to unravel the molecular landscape of cancer. A pan-cancer co-expression network
analysis has identified hub genes that hold significant potential for predicting drug responses across multiple      
malignancies [^10.5281_zenodo.2574643]. In colorectal cancer, comprehensive RNA-seq analysis of large cohorts has    
delineated differentially expressed genes enriched in cell cycle and DNA replication pathways, providing new         
therapeutic targets [^10.5281_zenodo.8307739]. Additionally, multi-omic prognostic modeling across thousands of      
